VECTOR

In C++, std::vector is a dynamic array that can automatically grow or shrink in size as elements are added or removed during program execution. It is part of the C++ Standard Template Library (STL) and provides a flexible, efficient alternative to traditional fixed-size arrays.

Vectors provide various member functions to manage their elements:

Function                  Description

push_back(value)          Adds an element to the end of the vector.

pop_back()                Removes the last element of the vector.

size()                     Returns the number of elements currently in the vector.

capacity()                  Returns the total storage space currently allocated.


