GL_POLYGON

GL_POLYGON is a primitive type used in legacy OpenGL (specifically within glBegin() and glEnd() sequences) to draw a single, filled convex polygon using a specified list of vertices. It is not a functional command on its own, but rather a constant passed to glBegin() to define how vertex data should be interpreted.

Key Details of GL_POLYGON

• Purpose: Draws a filled convex polygon.

• Requirements: Requires at least three vertices (e.g., a triangle) to draw.

• Vertex Ordering: Vertices should typically be provided in a clockwise direction, as this affects front-facing/back-facing, especially with lighting.

• Concave/Self-Intersecting Polygons: GL_POLYGON only supports convex polygons. Drawing concave or self-intersecting polygons will produce incorrect or unexpected results.
